   "line": 3,
   "message": "Step 2 tells the public that \"Each write waits for a confirm\". Step 1 says agents write through MCP. Only chat's pending-action confirm holds a write until someone approves it. A write tool called over /api/mcp runs straight away. The module standard says a `service: null` write \"still works over MCP but never becomes a chat card\", and packages/mcp/src/registry.ts has no confirm step. So the page tells prospects that agent writes are gated when they are not, which breaks AC-3 (\"Every claim matches PRODUCT.md or shipped modules\"). The prose check in marketing-areas.test.ts only looks for Coming words in HERO_LEDE, DESCRIPTION and the live claims, so it cannot catch a wrong claim about how the product behaves. Fix: reword the step so the confirm applies to chat only, for example \"In chat, amax asks before it changes anything. Every write, from chat, MCP or the UI, is permission-checked, audited and attributed\". Make the same change to the mock's step 2.",
   "original_severity": "major",
